    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7pXmso",
      "title": "Rotate two signers on the Foundation Upgrade and Operations safes (055-058)",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 1479,
      "body": "Rotates two owners on the Foundation Upgrade Safe (FUS, `0x847B5c174615B1B7fDF770882256e2D3E95b9D92`) and the Foundation Operations Safe (FOS, `0x9BA6e03D8B90dE867373Db8cF1A58d2F7F006b3A`), both 5-of-7:\n\n- `0xBF93D4d727F7Ba1F753E1124C3e532dCb04Ea2c8` → `0x7F1D4FE689B73B628285454667B93cfd09409f27`\n- `0x6419F81580343DF023E68715C6e269aFb00a2cc7` → `0xf1EfbdC2C0BDC4554E0f1639D7fe88cD870a4639`\n\nThreshold and owner count are unchanged.\n\nBoth owners are swapped on each safe, but rather than one transaction per safe, this is split into four single-`swapOwner` tasks, in execution order:\n\n1. `055-fus-rotation-1` — FUS, removes `0xBF93D4d727F7Ba1F753E1124C3e532dCb04Ea2c8` and adds `0x7F1D4FE689B73B628285454667B93cfd09409f27`\n2. `056-fus-rotation-2` — FUS, removes `0x6419F81580343DF023E68715C6e269aFb00a2cc7` and adds `0xf1EfbdC2C0BDC4554E0f1639D7fe88cD870a4639`; `0x7F1D4FE689B73B628285454667B93cfd09409f27` must be one of the signers\n3. `057-fos-rotation-1` — FOS, removes `0x6419F81580343DF023E68715C6e269aFb00a2cc7` and adds `0xf1EfbdC2C0BDC4554E0f1639D7fe88cD870a4639`\n4. `058-fos-rotation-2` — FOS, removes `0xBF93D4d727F7Ba1F753E1124C3e532dCb04Ea2c8` and adds `0x7F1D4FE689B73B628285454667B93cfd09409f27`; `0xf1EfbdC2C0BDC4554E0f1639D7fe88cD870a4639` must be one of the signers\n\nOne `swapOwner` per task for two reasons: (1) smaller blast radius per signing, and (2) it lets us sequence the tasks so each new owner must sign a later task before we depend on it. After a task adds a new owner to a safe, that owner is required to be one of the five signers on the next task for that safe. This produces a real Safe signature from each new key during the rotation, validating the key works. If a new key can't sign, we find out now rather than in a future ceremony.\n\nEach task's `VALIDATION.md` includes the expected domain and message hashes and the full state diff. These are simple Safe owner swaps rather than OPCM upgrades, so the state diff is small enough to enumerate in full.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-22T20:57:20Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 617,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7oaKKL",
      "title": "Require SIGNATURES for just execute",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 1477,
      "body": "`just execute` now fails before reading task config when `SIGNATURES` is unset or empty.\n\nThis prevents accidental bare execution from silently falling back to `0x`, while preserving the explicit pre-approved path:\n\n- `SIGNATURES=<hex signatures> just execute` for signed execution\n- `SIGNATURES=0x just execute` only after onchain approvals already exist, e.g. nested-safe execution after `just approve`\n\nValidation:\n- `env -u SIGNATURES just --justfile /private/tmp/superchain-ops-signatures-guard/src/justfile execute` exits with the new required-`SIGNATURES` error\n- `SIGNATURES= just --justfile /private/tmp/superchain-ops-signatures-guard/src/justfile execute` exits with the new empty-`SIGNATURES` error\n- `just --summary --justfile src/justfile`\n- `git diff --check HEAD~1 HEAD`\n\nI did not run an end-to-end broadcast execute; this PR only changes the preflight handling before the existing execute flow starts.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-19T14:23:00Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 11,
      "deletions": 1
    },
